WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:11.952
After the story, Onatah brought Magua a drink.

2
00:00:11.953 --> 00:00:14.144
He looked much better.

3
00:00:14.145 --> 00:00:16.972
"How many families live here?"

4
00:00:16.973 --> 00:00:20.800
asked Mandy, looking around.

5
00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:25.482
"Our longhouse has six families," said Onatah.

6
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:30.134
"I live with my grandmother, aunts, uncles, and cousins."

7
00:00:30.135 --> 00:00:32.876
A man entered the home.

8
00:00:32.877 --> 00:00:36.119
He whispered something to Clan Mother.

9
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.081
She looked very serious.

10
00:00:39.082 --> 00:00:45.891
"Onatah, take Vinnie and Mandy to the Green Corn dance," Clan Mother said.

11
00:00:45.892 --> 00:00:49.942
"What's wrong, Grandmother?" asked Onatah.

12
00:00:49.943 --> 00:00:55.886
"Don't worry. Go out and join the others," said Clan Mother.

13
00:00:55.887 --> 00:00:58.877
"I will call you when I need you."

14
00:00:58.878 --> 00:01:02.137
The children left the longhouse.

15
00:01:02.138 --> 00:01:08.833
"Everyone calls your grandmother 'Clan Mother,'" said Mandy. "Why?"

16
00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.214
"Women head all our families.

17
00:01:11.215 --> 00:01:15.021
Women are wise," said Onatah.

18
00:01:15.022 --> 00:01:19.038
"People always come to my grandmother for advice.

19
00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:22.411
She is the oldest woman in our clan."

20
00:01:22.412 --> 00:01:27.136
Mandy thought of the other places she had visited.

21
00:01:27.137 --> 00:01:31.274
Men were always the most important ones.

22
00:01:31.275 --> 00:01:36.745
Among the Iroquois, women were more respected than men.

23
00:01:36.746 --> 00:01:41.349
Many people were gathered in the middle of the village.

24
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.343
Everyone looked excited.

25
00:01:44.344 --> 00:01:48.851
The dancers were dressed in colorful clothes.

26
00:01:48.852 --> 00:01:52.476
Some were holding feathers in their hands.

27
00:01:52.477 --> 00:01:55.359
Others wore them in their hair.

28
00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.142
People were singing and playing small drums.

29
00:01:59.143 --> 00:02:03.418
"We thank you for the harvest," people sang.

30
00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:08.022
"We planted. We gathered. We ate."

31
00:02:08.023 --> 00:02:14.386
The dancers pretended to plant corn, beans, and squash.

32
00:02:14.387 --> 00:02:21.621
"Iroquois always plant the Three Sisters together in a small pile of soil," said Onatah.

33
00:02:21.622 --> 00:02:26.873
"And we use the shoulder blades of deer as hoes."

34
00:02:26.874 --> 00:02:30.051
Then Onatah jumped into the dance.

35
00:02:30.052 --> 00:02:33.337
Vinnie and Mandy did too.

36
00:02:33.338 --> 00:02:38.405
The rhythm of the loud drums matched the beat of their hearts.

37
00:02:38.406 --> 00:02:42.137
Everyone was smiling and laughing.

38
00:02:42.138 --> 00:02:46.335
After the dance, Onatah's grandmother spoke.

39
00:02:46.336 --> 00:02:50.743
"Something important has happened," said Clan Mother.

40
00:02:50.744 --> 00:02:53.457
"We must get ready for the council.

41
00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:55.481
They are coming."

42
00:02:55.482 --> 00:02:58.340
The people began to whisper.

43
00:02:58.341 --> 00:03:01.877
"The council?" asked Mandy.

44
00:03:01.878 --> 00:03:07.082
"Remember the story Grandmother told you?" said Onatah.

45
00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:12.047
"Deganawidah chose fifty chiefs to look after the Iroquois.

46
00:03:12.048 --> 00:03:14.813
Each nation has ten chiefs.

47
00:03:14.814 --> 00:03:19.936
They come together to make important decisions for the Iroquois."

48
00:03:19.937 --> 00:03:22.755
Onatah looked at her grandmother.

49
00:03:22.756 --> 00:03:27.209
Clan Mother looked sadly at Vinnie and Mandy.

50
00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:30.736
"What is it?" asked Mandy.

51
00:03:30.737 --> 00:03:36.135
"The whites have come into our land," Clan Mother sighed.

52
00:03:36.136 --> 00:03:39.068
"A fight may begin soon."

53
00:03:39.069 --> 00:03:43.336
Vinnie and Mandy looked at each other.

54
00:03:43.337 --> 00:03:48.624
"Maybe we should call Deganawidah's name," said Vinnie.

55
00:03:48.625 --> 00:03:50.875
"He promised to return."

56
00:03:50.876 --> 00:03:54.870
Clan Mother smiled and patted him lightly.

57
00:03:54.871 --> 00:03:58.543
"We will wait to hear from the council."

58
00:03:58.544 --> 00:04:02.066
Everyone stood near the central fire.

59
00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:04.359
People looked worried.

60
00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:08.005
No one danced or laughed anymore.

61
00:04:08.006 --> 00:04:12.440
"When are the chiefs coming?" asked Mandy nervously.

62
00:04:12.441 --> 00:04:14.508
"Will it be soon?"

63
00:04:14.509 --> 00:04:23.180
No one answered her.
